ll but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Mar (calmest seas, clearest skies, 200ft+ viz; Dec24-Jan1 crowded/expensive spike)","shoulder":"Nov (~25-40% off Dec) and May (~20-30% off April); near-peak conditions","green":"May-Sep warmest water ~27-28C / calmest seas; summer humidity + hurricane risk Jun-Nov (peak Aug-Oct)","booking_window_lead_time":"peak dive weeks book well ahead; Chinchorro multi-day + private crewed dive-yacht = book months ahead (limited weather windows / small vessels)","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green-summer value story: warmest/calmest water + 20-40% off rooms, thinner crowds, pair with hurricane trip insurance","holiday_event_peaks":["Cozumel Carnival 2026: main parades Feb 14/15/17 (Fat Tue), run Feb 11-18, pre-Carnival Jan 17-Feb 8; floats with pre-Lenten lunar calendar","cruise-ship day-crowds congest San Miguel + nearer reefs — push early boats / south-zone sites"],"campaign_start_trigger":"open peak-season campaign Aug-Sep for Dec-Mar; shoulder push Sep-Oct (Nov) and Feb-Mar (May); Carnival micro-campaign Nov-Dec for mid-Feb"},"jewels":[{"name":"Palancar Reef (Gardens/Caves/Bricks/Horseshoe)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"2-tank day-boat dive","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","commission":"dive-op DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Santa Rosa Wall","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive (expert-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Columbia Deep","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive","tier":"comfort","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Banco Chinchorro atoll","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"future","bookable":"multi-day/liveaboard-style from Xcalak/Mahahual","tier":"premier","source":"http://www.pelagiclife.org/chinchorro","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"Aggressor/liveaboard reseller = Commissioned Agent on application"},{"name":"Palancar snorkel + El Cielo sandbar","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","bookable":"catamaran/snorkel tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","si":"ocean","blurb":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","commission":"Viator/GYG affiliate + DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cozumel?","a":"Decompression discipline, not crime — this is a repetitive multi-day dive island. Follow DAN''s no-fly windows strictly (12h single, 18h multi-day, 24h conservative), because Cozumel''s day-boat profiles stack dives fast; the island has multiple chambers, but a bad no-fly call is the classic mistake. Also plan for dengue (repellent), bottled water and hurricane season (Jun–Nov).","source":"dan.org / travel.state.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is drift diving in Cozumel dangerous?","a":"No, when you take the drift briefing seriously — but it is not passive. Expect a near-constant ~1.5-knot current that does the swimming for you; do a controlled descent, stay with the group and dive master, deploy an SMB, and dive within your certification. Santa Rosa Wall is expert-only; Palancar Gardens suits most certified divers.","source":"cozumelscuba.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the best dive sites in Cozumel, and can beginners dive them?","a":"Palancar Gardens is the everyone-friendly classic — coral pinnacles, archways and swim-throughs at 100-ft-plus visibility with mild current — while Santa Rosa Wall and Columbia Deep are advanced drifts. Beginners and newly certified divers do best at Palancar; Santa Rosa, dropping from ~15 m into the blue, is expert-only.","source":"torntackies.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I do a liveaboard from Cozumel?","a":"Not from Cozumel itself — it is a day-boat island. True liveaboard-style multi-day diving goes to Banco Chinchorro, ~30–35 nm off Costa Maya, launched from Xcalak or Mahahual to the south, not Cozumel. The luxury alternative near Cozumel is a private crewed dive-yacht charter, since overnight liveaboards are effectively banned inside the national park.","source":"pelagiclife.org / islandlifemexico.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can non-divers snorkel Cozumel, and what''s the reef fee?","a":"Yes — the reef is superb for snorkelers, from Palancar shallows to the El Cielo starfish sandbar by catamaran. Everyone entering the marine park pays the reef bracelet, MX$220 (~US$13) per person per day as of Jan 2026; snorkel tours carry no no-fly restriction, making them a good last-day option before a flight.","source":"cozumelmio.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is Cozumel good for a honeymoon or a couples'' dive trip?","a":"Yes — it pairs world-class diving with real staffed villas. Luxury Cozumel and Villa Experience run oceanfront staffed homes (chef, concierge) from ~US$450/night, and there is no branded ultra flag on-island, so for hotel-brand luxury couples ferry to Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree) ~an hour away.","source":"luxurycozumel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Cozumel?","a":"December–March is peak, with the calmest seas, clearest skies and legendary 200-ft-plus visibility. November and May are the value sweet spots — near-peak conditions at ~25–40% (Nov) and ~20–30% (May) below Dec rates; May–September brings the warmest, calmest water (~27–28°C) but summer humidity and hurricane risk.","source":"sunsetcozumel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cozumel Diving: Drift the Mesoamerican Reef","meta_description":"Cozumel is the Caribbean''s drift-diving crown - Palancar, Santa Rosa Wall and the Mesoamerican Reef, with chambers, no-fly rules and the Chinchorro liveaboard hook.","slug":"cozumel-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cozumel drift diving","long_tail":["Cozumel dive sites Palancar Santa Rosa","Cozumel marine park fee 2026","Banco Chinchorro liveaboard","Cozumel recompression chamber","Mesoamerican Barrier Reef diving"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["buceo en Cozumel","arrecife Palancar Santa Rosa","camara hiperbarica Cozumel","buceo de deriva Cozumel","Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel","Banco Chinchorro buceo","villa privada de lujo Cozumel"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"liveaboard","status":"future","note":"Cozumel = day-boat reef diving; liveaboard/multi-day runs to Banco Chinchorro launch from Xcalak/Mahahual, NOT Cozumel"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private Paradise Villa","location":"Cozumel (on-island)","what":"oceanfront exclusive-use villa, sleeps up to 24, 40+ staff incl. 7 rotating chefs + British-butler-trained butlers","why_ultra":"full-buyout fully-staffed private-resort — the on-island ultra expression","earning":"villa-agency/DMC commission on application (agent-of-record; no net-rate resale)","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a standalone; attach Virtuoso mainland stay for perks","mor_posture":"clean agent-side; red-flag any villa-inventory mark-up","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://privateparadisevilla.com/"},{"name":"Private crewed dive-yacht charter","location":"Cozumel / Riviera Maya (on-water)","what":"fully-crewed private yacht (captain+deckhand+dive master, chef/hostess on premium boats), 15+ sites + El Cielo, premium open bar","why_ultra":"ultra dive expression; only luxury ''liveaboard-style'' the park''s vessel-size rules allow (overnight liveaboards effectively banned in-park)","earning":"charter/DMC commission on application","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a direct; pair with Virtuoso stay","mor_posture":"agent-of-record on charter; no net-rate resale","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://dayyachtcharters.com/cozumel-yacht-charters-luxury-boat-rentals.html"},{"name":"Riviera Maya branded ultra (Rosewood/Banyan Tree Mayakoba, Chable Maroma, Maroma Belmond)","location":"Riviera Maya mainland (ferry + short transfer)","what":"Forbes/branded ultra-luxury resorts + villas; private pools, top spas, PGA course","why_ultra":"nearest true branded ultra flag — no ultra flag on Cozumel itself","earning":"Virtuoso preferred rate + commission (or via host-Virtuoso)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade, daily breakfast for two, early check-in/late check-out, ~US$100 credit, VIP welcome (Mayakoba flags)","mor_posture":"standard Virtuoso agent-of-record","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/mayakoba-riviera-maya"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cozumel, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.423,"lng":-86.9223}}'::jsonb, 11),
  ('east-cape-mexico', '10S', 'East Cape (Cabo del Este)', 'Mexico', 'The wild Sea-of-Cortez side of Cabo', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"romance","expedition","diveglobal","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Costa Palmas spans 1,500 acres with 3 km of swimmable Sea-of-Cortez beach, ~45 min from SJD airport (Source: costapalmas.com, 2026-07-04)","Prime sportfishing May–early Nov: blue/black/striped marlin, sailfish, dorado, wahoo, yellowfin tuna (Source: marinalife.com, 2026-07-04)","El Norte wind peaks Dec–Mar at 15–25 kt; Los Barriles is a top-tier kite/windsurf beach (Source: middlecasa.com, 2026-07-04)","Whales present in Baja waters late Dec–early Apr, offshore in the Sea of Cortez (Source: oceanicsociety.org, 2026-07-04)","Cabo Pulmo NP: 7,111-ha no-take reserve ~30 km from Los Barriles; +462% fish abundance by 2010 (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_Pulmo_National_Park, 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital H+ Los Cabos (Km 24.5, 624-104-9300, ~45+ min) or La Paz (~2.5 hr); local East Cape Health Center Los Barriles is daytime clinic only","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry, whales late Dec–early Apr, El Norte wind Dec–Mar)","shoulder":"May & Oct–Nov (fishing ramp, pre/post-heat)","green":"Jul–Sep (hottest + hurricane window Jun–Nov; peak billfish/dorado)","booking_lead":"6–12 mo Costa Palmas ultra & holiday villas; 1–3 mo peak fishing charters (verify)","off_season_specials":"green-season fishing packages + villa value windows; Van Wormer customizable group packages 2–200","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year & Easter (Costa Palmas holiday premium); Lord of the Wind kite/windsurf showdown (January, Los Barriles)","campaign_start":"Aug–Sep for Nov–Apr Romance/whale peak; Mar–Apr for May–Nov fishing; Sep–Oct for kite/windsurf"},"jewels":[{"name":"Costa Palmas beachfront (3 km swimmable sea)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"rare swimmable Cabo-side beach with two ultra brands on one estate","bookable_category":"resort/villa","tier":"ultra","source":"https://costapalmas.com/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"romance","blurb":"rare swimmable Cabo-side beach with two ultra brands on one estate","commission":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner + host-Virtuoso; MoR villa","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Casa Blake (Marina Village)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"boutique hotel + condo pied-à-terre at the marina heart","bookable_category":"hotel/residence","tier":"luxury","source":"https://costapalmas.com/overview/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"romance","blurb":"boutique hotel + condo pied-à-terre at the marina heart","commission":"agency/host","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Sea-of-Cortez whale season","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"offshore gray/humpback/blue/fin whales in one of Earth''s richest whale seas","bookable_category":"day tour / private charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.oceanicsociety.org/travel-ideas/best-whale-watching-in-baja-the-complete-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"expedition","blurb":"offshore gray/humpback/blue/fin whales in one of Earth''s richest whale seas","commission":"activity affiliate (~4–8%) or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"East Cape billfish grounds","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"legendary marlin/dorado/wahoo/tuna variety, billfish year-round","bookable_category":"fishing charter","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.marinalife.com/articles/fishing-mexicos-east-cape + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"legendary marlin/dorado/wahoo/tuna variety, billfish year-round","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/Van Wormer fishing desk","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Roosterfish inshore","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"iconic catch-and-release inshore fight; global rooster hotspot","bookable_category":"panga charter","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.marinalife.com/articles/fishing-mexicos-east-cape + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"iconic catch-and-release inshore fight; global rooster hotspot","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"local operator","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Los Barriles kite/windsurf (El Norte)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"15–25 kt afternoons Dec–Mar; Lord of the Wind in January","bookable_category":"school/camp + hotel package","tier":"comfort","source":"https://middlecasa.com/why-los-barriles-is-mexicos-winter-mecca-for-kitesurfers/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"ocean","blurb":"15–25 kt afternoons Dec–Mar; Lord of the Wind in January","commission":"activity affiliate / lesson package","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Cabo Pulmo reef (cross-link, own dossier)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","hook":"20,000-yr-old richest reef on NA west coast; +462% fish abundance recovery","bookable_category":"local dive op (lottery sites)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_Pulmo_National_Park + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"20,000-yr-old richest reef on NA west coast; +462% fish abundance recovery","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"local dive op; NP fees non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the East Cape a good honeymoon base?","a":"Yes — it holds two of Mexico''s most serious luxury resorts on one estate. Costa Palmas fronts a rare swimmable Cabo-side beach (3 km) with the Four Seasons and Amanvari, 45 minutes from SJD, so couples get calm water plus branded ultra away from the corridor crowds.","source":"costapalmas.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When can I see whales in the Sea of Cortez here?","a":"Late December to early April, with the blue-whale peak Feb–Apr. Gray, humpback, blue and fin whales all pass offshore, on day tours or private charters out of the East Cape — one of Earth''s richest whale seas.","source":"oceanicsociety.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the fishing and the wind best on the East Cape?","a":"Two opposite seasons: billfish and dorado peak May to early November in glass-calm water, while the El Norte wind turns Los Barriles into a 15–25 kt kite and windsurf arena Dec–March. Pick the season for the sport you came for.","source":"marinalife.com / middlecasa.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"East Cape Baja (Costa Palmas) Travel Guide — Fishing, Whales & Ultra-Luxury | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The wild Sea-of-Cortez side of Cabo: Costa Palmas ultra (Four Seasons + Amanvari), world-class marlin/dorado sportfishing, Los Barriles kite season, whales Dec–Apr, and the Cabo Pulmo reef.","slug":"east-cape-mexico","primary_keywords":["East Cape Baja","Costa Palmas","East Cape sportfishing","Los Barriles kiteboarding","Four Seasons Los Cabos Costa Palmas"],"long_tail":["best time to fish East Cape Baja","whale watching Sea of Cortez December April","Amanvari Aman Costa Palmas","luxury villa rental East Cape","Cabo Pulmo diving from Los Barriles"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["Cabo del Este Baja","Costa Palmas Los Cabos","pesca deportiva Cabo del Este","kitesurf Los Barriles El Norte","avistamiento de ballenas Mar de Cortés","buceo Cabo Pulmo","villas de lujo Cabo del Este"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Resort Los Cabos at Costa Palmas","why_ultra":"141-room flagship + beachfront residences on private 1,500-acre estate, swimmable beach, RTJ II golf","earning":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner or via host-Virtuoso (never fabricate %)","virtuoso_value_add":"daily breakfast for two, ~$100 resort credit, upgrade priority, early check-in/late check-out, ~$495 airport transfer, VIP recognition","mor":"MoR on villa rentals"},{"name":"Amanvari (Aman, Costa Palmas)","why_ultra":"first Aman in Mexico; intimate 18-key + 4–7BR Aman Residences (13k–20k sq ft), Aman Spa, private beach","earning":"on application / via host-Aman-preferred (never fabricate %)","virtuoso_value_add":"per Aman preferred-partner program","mor":"MoR on residences"},{"name":"Costa Palmas Marina & residences","why_ultra":"only Four Seasons + Aman branded marina in Los Cabos; superyacht harbor up to ~250 ft; Marina Village","earning":"real-estate/rental via host","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a (property/marina)","mor":"MoR"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"East Cape (Cabo del Este), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":23.68,"lng":-109.7,"note":"approx Los Barriles / La Ribera–Costa Palmas corridor"}}'::jsonb, 12),
  ('fernando-de-noronha-brazil', '10S', 'Fernando de Noronha, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Volcanic archipelago, marine sanctuary, dolphin dawn', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Northeast Beaches & Bahia', '{"liveaboard","tropical","romance","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_why":"mainland urban crime + kidnapping; favelas L4. Archipelago itself is low-risk controlled-access marine park.","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"FEN via Recife (REC) or Natal (NAT) only — Gol/Azul","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24h surface interval before FEN->mainland flight; plan dive-free last day","hyperbaric_chamber_onisland":true,"hyperbaric_note":"chamber adjacent to Hospital Sao Lucas (basic care); serious trauma/complex DCI requires mainland evac (Recife/Natal); weather can delay","remote_flag":true,"ocean_hazards":["strong currents/swell at outer-sea pinnacles & deep sites","riptides (worst Dec-Mar)","equatorial sun"],"protected_no_entry":["Baia dos Golfinhos (dolphin resting bay)"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"dive_calendar":true,"peak_dive":"Aug-Nov (viz apex Sep-Oct)","peak_surf_highseason":"Dec-Mar","inflection":["late July","late November"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-late July for dive peak; mid-late November for Dec-Mar season)","booking_lead":"3-6 months for Dec-Mar (visitor cap + eco-tax + park permit)","offseason_fill":"Apr-Jun (rain hits surface, reef viz stays strong — diver''s value window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Baia do Sancho","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"park ticket (pass-through) + commissionable boat/DMC day"},{"name":"Forte Boldro sunset viewpoint","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","source":"https://postcardfromtaylor.com/blog/brazil/noronha-beaches/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"year-round","commission":"guided island tour add-on"},{"name":"Ilha-tour boat trip","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/fernando-de-noronha-diving-and-snorkeling/","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"commissionable boat operator/DMC"},{"name":"Corveta Ipiranga wreck (~62m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/naufragio-da-corveta-ipiranga-no-arquipelago-de-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"premium tech-dive package"},{"name":"Caverna de Sapata (~18m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"guided reef-dive package"},{"name":"Atalaia dive/snorkel zone (8-22m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"dive-operator day trip"},{"name":"Baia dos Golfinhos dawn watch","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"expedition","commission":"guided dawn eco-tour (no-entry viewpoint)"},{"name":"Atalaia natural pool (guided/capped)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.parnanoronha.com.br/en/atrativos","hook":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","si":"expedition","blurb":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","commission":"ICMBio permit (pass-through) + guided eco add-on"},{"name":"Projeto Tamar visitor center","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/projeto-tamar-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"expedition","commission":"eco-tour visit inside guided day"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to dive Fernando de Noronha?","a":"August–November is the dive peak because the dry season delivers the clearest water and calmest seas, with the September–October visibility apex reaching up to ~50 m. April–June (rainy) is the diver''s value window — rain hits the surface, not the reef, so visibility stays strong and the island is quieter.","source":"planetaexo.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How do you get to Baía do Sancho?","a":"Baía do Sancho is reached only by boat or by a staircase carved into the volcanic rock face, and a marine-park pass is required. It has been voted the best beach in the world by TripAdvisor travelers five times, which is why access is deliberately controlled.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which is the best honeymoon pousada on Fernando de Noronha?","a":"Pousada Maravilha is consistently ranked the island''s top honeymoon hotel, with six sea-facing apartments plus bungalows with private hot tubs, an infinity pool, fine dining and a spa. Nannai Noronha (10 bungalows, private verandas, direct beach access) is the other ultra-tier couples pick.","source":"boutiquetravelexperts.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you swim with the spinner dolphins at Baía dos Golfinhos?","a":"No — Baía dos Golfinhos is a no-entry protected dolphin resting bay: no descending, no swimming, no boats inside. Spinner dolphins are watched from a clifftop viewpoint, best at first light. This is a legal protection, not a suggestion.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Remoteness and medical evacuation. Fernando de Noronha has a hyperbaric chamber adjacent to Hospital São Lucas, but the hospital provides basic emergency care only — serious trauma or complex decompression illness requires evacuation to the mainland (Recife/Natal), and weather can delay the flight. Carry insurance with medevac and dive conservatively.","source":"divejourney.io, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving the Corveta Ipiranga wreck dangerous?","a":"It is technical / Extended-Range diving: the wreck sits at ~62 m off Ponta da Sapata, so operators require Nitrox plus ~50 logged dives and evaluation dives before permitting it, always with a pro. Recreational divers stay on shallower 8–22 m reef and cave sites. Because you leave only by air, observe an 18–24 h surface interval before your flight.","source":"bahia.ws, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"search_language":"pt-BR","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Fernando de Noronha mergulho","Baia do Sancho","taxa ambiental Noronha","taxa de preservacao ambiental Noronha 2026","Pousada Maravilha lua de mel","piscina natural Atalaia"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Pousada Maravilha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + AOR; MoR on buyout","note":"island''s top honeymoon property"},{"name":"Nannai Noronha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + dive attach; MoR villa-equivalent"},{"name":"Pousada Ze Maria","tier":"premier","lane":"premium romance","earning":"commissionable pousada + dining attach"},{"name":"Pousada Teju-Acu","tier":"premier","lane":"eco-luxury","earning":"commissionable boutique pousada + eco-tour attach"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Fernando de Noronha, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.8547,"lng":-32.4248}}'::jsonb, 13),
  ('galapagos-islands-ecuador', '10S', 'The Galápagos Islands', 'Ecuador', 'Liveaboard weeks and island crossings', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"liveaboard","expedition"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Darwin and Wolf islands are reachable ONLY by liveaboard; most trips run 7 nights with up to 4 dives/day.","Galapagos is one of the only places on earth to reliably dive with whale sharks (10-12m adults), June-November, peak August-September.","During the June-November cool season ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve; schools aggregate along the thermocline ~20-30m.","Galapagos National Park entry fee doubled to US$200 per foreign adult on 2024-08-01; INGALA/CGREG transit card (TCT) is a separate ~US$20-30.","Access is via Baltra/Seymour (GPS) or San Cristobal (SCY) on Avianca/LATAM flights from Quito (UIO) or Guayaquil (GYE) only."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Puerto Ayora, Santa Cruz — Protesub S.A. / SSS Recompression Chamber Network (DAN referral center), 24/7, +593 5 252-6911. Only chamber in the islands; many hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf; serious cases medevac to mainland or US.","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_date":"2025-10-14","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) / T (Terrorism) / U (Unrest) / K (Kidnapping) — mainland-driven; islands not a named area","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":"none (BIN 4 — standard L2 disclosure only)","l2_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"Galápagos and Quito explicitly NOT designated restricted; L4 zones are mainland-only (Esmeraldas city+north, Guayaquil south of Portete de Tarqui Ave., Duran, Huaquillas/Arenillas, Quevedo/Quinsaloma/Pueblo Viejo)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"GPS (Baltra/Seymour) and SCY (San Cristobal) via UIO (Quito) or GYE (Guayaquil) on Avianca/LATAM","no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before the island-to-mainland flight (note Quito altitude ~2,850m)","medevac_note":"State Dept warns serious illness/injury typically requires medical evacuation; recommends evacuation insurance $60,000+","other":"open-Pacific seasickness (long overnight Darwin/Wolf crossings roughest); extreme equatorial sun; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Coastal Region FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabí Santa Elena Guayas El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar-two-season","dive_calendar":true,"warm_snorkel_season":"December-May (warmer water ~25-27C, calm seas, best snorkel/land wildlife; family + honeymoon)","big_marine_dive_season":"June-November (cool ~16-24C, strong currents; hammerhead schools + whale sharks at Darwin & Wolf)","peak":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","dive_curve_start":"2026-06-01","warm_curve_start":"2026-12-01","booking_lead_months":"6-12 (top liveaboard cabins + premium expedition suites; whale-shark weeks and holidays sell first)","shoulder_off_season_fill":"April-May and September-October","fire_date":"2026-05-18","trigger_date":"2026-05-18","secondary_fire_date":"2026-11-15","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor / expedition-cruise availability feeds + hammerhead & whale-shark sighting logs; upwelling onset and pelagic aggregation shift yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"Darwin''s Arch / Darwin Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.naturetripper.com/articles/whale-sharks-galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Galápagos Aggressor III) — the moat"},{"name":"Wolf Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.dive-the-world.com/posts/darwin-wolf/galapagos-islands-diving-trips-darwin-and-wolf-islands.php","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane — the moat"},{"name":"Gordon Rocks (off Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-boat from Puerto Ayora"},{"name":"Kicker Rock / León Dormido (off San Cristóbal)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.oars.com/adventures/galapagos-origins-of-species/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-operator from San Cristóbal"},{"name":"Cabo Marshall / Cabo Douglas & Punta Vicente Roca (Isabela/Fernandina)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Bartolomé — Pinnacle Rock","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Española — Punta Suárez (waved albatross)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","when":"year-round","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Genovesa — Bird Island","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Charles Darwin Research Station + giant tortoises (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Ayora","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane add-on to a Fora hotel/cruise booking"},{"name":"Isabela — Sierra Negra volcano & Galápagos penguins","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","si":"expedition","commission":"AFF day-operator lane; Fora if bundled in a land package"},{"name":"Los Túneles (Cabo Rosa, Isabela)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF day-operator lane"},{"name":"Tortuga Bay (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane (self-guided) add-on to a Fora hotel booking"}],"faq":[{"q":"How dangerous is diving Darwin and Wolf — can beginners do it?","a":"No — these are advanced dives, not a beginner destination. Reputable operators gate Darwin/Wolf on Advanced Open Water certification plus logged current/cold-water experience: divers hook onto ledges in ripping current at 20–30 m in 16–24 °C water, far from support. Gordon Rocks and Kicker Rock are the intermediate-to-advanced warm-ups.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How long should I wait to fly after diving the Galápagos?","a":"Plan a full 18–24 hours before the island-to-mainland flight. A liveaboard week is repetitive multi-day diving (DAN: 18 h minimum, 24 h recommended), and Quito sits at ~2,850 m — so never book a same-day-as-last-dive flight. The only hyperbaric chamber is in Puerto Ayora, hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf, so DAN evacuation insurance is effectively mandatory.","source":"DAN guidance via sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"dive-safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive for hammerheads and whale sharks?","a":"June–November — the cool, plankton-rich season — is the big-animal window, with whale sharks peaking August–September, because the Humboldt upwelling drops water to 16–24 °C and concentrates pelagic life; ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve then, schooling in the hundreds. Expect cooler water and stronger current.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Do I need a cruise, or can I stay on land?","a":"Both work, but the iconic sites need a boat. Darwin and Wolf are liveaboard-only, and by park rule every visitor-site landing must be led by a licensed naturalist guide. Land-based island-hopping (Santa Cruz, Isabela) covers tortoises, Tortuga Bay and day dives; the deep wildlife (Española albatross, Genovesa seabirds) needs an expedition cruise.","source":"oars.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the best Galápagos trip for a honeymoon?","a":"A small all-suite expedition yacht or the highlands Pikaia Lodge. The warm season (Dec–May, water 25–27 °C, calm seas) is the easiest for first-timers and snorkeling; book 6–12 months ahead because the top cabins and suites — and holiday sailings — sell out first.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com / dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Galápagos Diving & Expedition Cruises — Darwin & Wolf Liveaboards, Hammerheads, Whale Sharks | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["Galapagos liveaboard diving","Darwin Wolf hammerheads","Galapagos cruise","Galapagos whale shark diving","Galapagos Aggressor III","best time to dive Galapagos","Galapagos expedition cruise","islas Galápagos crucero","bucear Galápagos","crucero de buceo Galápagos","tiburón ballena Galápagos","no fly after diving Galapagos"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Aqua Mare (Aqua Expeditions) — 16-guest superyacht","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane; full-yacht buyout = villa-equivalent","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Silversea Silver Origin — 100-guest ultra-luxury expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Virtuoso-preferred)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Celebrity Flora — 100-guest all-suite expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Ecoventura Origin / Theory / Evolve — 20-guest all-suite (Relais & Châteaux)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Relais & Châteaux)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Pikaia Lodge (Santa Cruz highlands, Relais & Châteaux + private yacht)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA)","source":"https://www.mrandmrssmith.com/luxury-hotels/pikaia-lodge"},{"name":"Private full-yacht charter (Aggressor III buyout / all-suite expedition buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/galapagos"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"The Galápagos Islands, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-0.9538,"lng":-90.9656}}'::jsonb, 14)
