  ('huatulco-mexico', '10S', 'Huatulco', 'Mexico', 'Oaxaca''s calm nine-bay coast', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Oaxaca (Oaxaca City & Coast)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","ocean","culture","wildlife","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Nine bays across 36 beaches; horseshoe coves stay calm for swimming/snorkeling — greener and calmer than surf-driven Puerto Escondido.","Huatulco National Park protects ~11,890 ha of coast, reef and forest; dolphins, turtles and seasonal whales.","Playa La Entrega is the best land-accessible snorkel cove — reef starts feet from shore.","Pluma Hidalgo (~1,350 m, 45 min inland) produces some of the Americas'' top high-altitude Arabica coffee.","Copalita is one of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico (with Tulum) — Zapotec/Mixtec city settled by ~500 BC.","Humpback whale season Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% sighting success at peak); olive-ridley/green turtle nesting Jul-Jan."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Local Huatulco/La Crucecita clinics stabilize routine cases; serious trauma routes to Oaxaca City or Mexico City for definitive/ICU care","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"L2 (Oaxaca) — Exercise Increased Caution (Huatulco explicitly unrestricted); updated May 29, 2026","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"malaria":"low/negligible in Huatulco tourist coast","dengue":"endemic seasonal risk, higher May-Nov; use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only; resort water filtered","swimming":"calmer/safer bays than Puerto Escondido, but open beaches carry riptides — swim sheltered coves","hurricane_season":"Pacific storm season ~Jun-Oct; insure/refundable","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season; sunny, no rain, highs 29-34C; whale window Dec-Mar)","inflection":"late Nov & April (shoulder value, still dry/sunny)","green":"May-Oct (rainy/low; hotter, lush, cheapest; overlaps turtle nesting)","whale_season":"humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21, 97% sighting success at peak","turtle_season":"olive-ridley/green nesting Jul-Jan; hatchling-release draw","fire_date":"early-to-mid November — 1-2 weeks ahead of the Dec 15 humpback curve-start / dry-season flip","holiday_event_peaks":["Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa","whale-watch Dec-Mar"],"fill_the_beds":"green months lead with Pluma Hidalgo coffee day, Copalita eco-archaeology + river rafting, turtle-release evenings, calm-bay snorkel, green-season all-inclusive value","campaign_start_trigger":"open peak/whale campaigns early-mid Nov; shoulder (late Nov, Apr) ~3-4 months out; turtle-nesting green-season value push Jul-Oct"},"jewels":[{"name":"Nine-Bays boat tour","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","hook":"Full-day boat expedition across the nine bays with beach + snorkel stops.","bookable_category":"guided boat tour","source":"https://www.amstardmc.com/en/excursions/sea-and-sun-bays/","si":"ocean","blurb":"Full-day boat expedition across the nine bays with beach + snorkel stops.","commission":"Amstar DMC ~12% / affiliate 4-8%; park bracelet pass-through"},{"name":"Bahia Maguey & Bahia Organo snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Calm-cove snorkel over close reef with beachfront seafood palapas at Maguey.","bookable_category":"boat snorkel stop","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Huatulco/Huatulco-National-Park-Sightseeing-Cruise-with-Snorkeling-in-Maguey-Bay/d4334-5885HUXSUN","si":"ocean","blurb":"Calm-cove snorkel over close reef with beachfront seafood palapas at Maguey.","commission":"affiliate / DMC ~12%; food pass-through"},{"name":"Playa La Entrega reef","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Land-accessible horseshoe cove — reef starts feet from shore, calm and current-sheltered.","bookable_category":"shore snorkel / rental","source":"https://mrplayas.com/blog/huatulco-oaxaca-guide","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Land-accessible horseshoe cove — reef starts feet from shore, calm and current-sheltered.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% on packaged tours; DIY non-commissionable"},{"name":"Whale & dolphin watch","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% success at peak); year-round dolphins/turtles.","bookable_category":"wildlife boat safari","source":"https://seasafarihuatulco.com/whale-watching-tours/","si":"wildlife","blurb":"Humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% success at peak); year-round dolphins/turtles.","commission":"operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Cacaluta & San Agustin remote bays","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Wild, undeveloped bays — heart-shaped Cacaluta and gin-clear San Agustin (18 m viz).","bookable_category":"private boat / dedicated tour","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g150789-d524145-Reviews-Bahia_de_Cacaluta-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Wild, undeveloped bays — heart-shaped Cacaluta and gin-clear San Agustin (18 m viz).","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC / operator affiliate; park bracelet pass-through"},{"name":"La Entrega / San Agustin reef dive","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Beginner-to-intermediate protected-reef dives; San Agustin ~30 m sunken ship.","bookable_category":"reef dive (PADI operator)","source":"https://www.explorehuatulco.com/Huatulco-Scuba-Diving-Guide","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Beginner-to-intermediate protected-reef dives; San Agustin ~30 m sunken ship.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"dive-operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Pluma Hidalgo coffee-finca day","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"45-min drive to ~1,350 m coffee country — finca tour, roasting, tasting, mirador views.","bookable_category":"guided coffee tour","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/huatulco-l781/huatulco-santa-maria-and-pluma-hidalgo-coffee-tour-t631983/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"45-min drive to ~1,350 m coffee country — finca tour, roasting, tasting, mirador views.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Copalita eco-archaeological park","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"One of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico — Zapotec/Mixtec city in rainforest above the river mouth.","bookable_category":"guided park visit / combo","source":"https://lugares.inah.gob.mx/en/node/4487","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"One of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico — Zapotec/Mixtec city in rainforest above the river mouth.","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC ~12%; park entry pass-through"},{"name":"La Crucecita zocalo + Church of Guadalupe","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Real Oaxacan town with a zocalo, market, and one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","bookable_category":"walking tour / DIY","source":"https://www.explorehuatulco.com/la-crucecita-region-huatulco-mexico","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Real Oaxacan town with a zocalo, market, and one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate on guided walks; DIY non-commissionable"},{"name":"Copalita River rafting","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"Guided whitewater at La Bocana beside the archaeological site; fuller in green months.","bookable_category":"guided rafting","source":"https://www.huatulcowatersports.com/tours/copalita-archaological-site-143783","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided whitewater at La Bocana beside the archaeological site; fuller in green months.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in the water?","a":"Riptides on the open beaches, not the sheltered bays. The horseshoe coves (La Entrega, Maguey, San Agustín) are genuinely calm and swimmable, but open stretches of Tangolunda and Chahué carry rip currents — swim only the flagged, sheltered coves, and heed the flags.","source":"mrplayas.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Which bays are calm enough for swimming and families?","a":"The horseshoe coves. La Entrega is the best land-accessible snorkel cove — the reef starts feet from shore — and Maguey, Órgano and San Agustín stay calm inside their coves; that''s the difference from surf-driven Puerto Escondido up the coast.","source":"mrplayas.com / secretflying.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What''s the one must-do day here?","a":"The nine-bays boat tour — a full-day (~7 h) expedition across the nine bays with beach and snorkel stops, bookable through Amstar''s \"Sea and Sun\"/\"Seven Bays\" excursions or affiliate marketplaces (the National Park conservation bracelet is a cash pass-through).","source":"amstardmc.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When can I see whales?","a":"Humpbacks run **Dec 15–Mar 21**, with sightings on **over 97% of tours** at the peak, on boat safaris out of Santa Cruz; dolphins and turtles are year-round, and turtle nesting (olive-ridley/green) runs Jul–Jan.","source":"oceanico.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Can beginners dive the reef here?","a":"Yes — the protected Pacific reef is beginner-friendly. La Entrega runs 10–12 m and San Agustín adds a ~30 m sunken ship for advanced divers, with up to ~18 m visibility in the dry season; book only PADI-certified operators (Huatulco Dive Center, Anfibios, Hurricane Divers).","source":"explorehuatulco.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is there culture beyond the beach?","a":"Yes — Copalita is one of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico (with Tulum), a Zapotec/Mixtec city settled by ~500 BC in rainforest above the river mouth, and La Crucecita''s zócalo holds one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","source":"lugares.inah.gob.mx, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Huatulco good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, for calm-bay romance rather than branded-ultra. Secrets Huatulco is the adults-only, all-oceanfront-suite anchor of the Tangolunda strip; the coast tops out at premier all-inclusive plus a top oceanfront villa in Conejos — there is no Aman/Rosewood-tier hotel here.","source":"hyattinclusivecollection.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Huatulco Travel Guide 2026 — Nine Bays, Snorkel & Coffee Country | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Huatulco, Oaxaca''s calm eco-resort coast: the nine-bays boat tour, Maguey/Organo snorkel, La Crucecita, Pluma Hidalgo coffee, Copalita eco-archaeology, whale season, Level 2 safety (Huatulco unrestricted).","slug":"huatulco-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Huatulco","Bahías de Huatulco","La Crucecita","tour de las nueve bahías Huatulco","snorkel en Bahía Maguey","café Pluma Hidalgo tour","Parque Eco-Arqueológico Copalita","avistamiento de ballenas Huatulco","mejor época para visitar Huatulco","buceo en Huatulco","villas frente al mar Conejos Huatulco"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Secrets Huatulco Resort & Spa","price_tier":"premier","virtuoso":false,"earning":"all-incl -> OA host AOR + Hyatt Inclusive TA ~12%","mor_posture":true,"note":"adults-only all-oceanfront-suite; the branded ceiling for the coast","source":"https://www.hyattinclusivecollection.com/en/resorts-hotels/secrets/mexico/huatulco-resort-spa/"},{"name":"Dreams Huatulco Resort & Spa","price_tier":"comfort-premier","virtuoso":false,"earning":"OA host AOR + Hyatt Inclusive TA ~12%","mor_posture":true,"note":"family sister with shared Secrets access","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g150789-d2089597-Reviews-Secrets_Huatulco_Resort_Spa-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html"},{"name":"Las Palmas Resort","price_tier":"comfort","virtuoso":false,"earning":"OA host AOR","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowTopic-g150789-i740-k14655958-Secrets_vs_Dreams_vs_Barcelo-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html"},{"name":"Boutique bay villas — Residencial Conejos (oceanfront)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / via host or DMC villa AOR","mor_posture":true,"note":"villa ceiling; no branded true-ultra hotel on this eco-resort coast; net-rate resale red","source":"https://www.airbnb.com/santa-maria-huatulco-mexico/stays/villas"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Huatulco, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":15.76,"lng":-96.13}}'::jsonb, 17),
