ing."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; highest rates, biggest crowds)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off, good weather)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane/low; cheapest; marina monitors weather)","marina_sportfishing_calendar":"charters year-round weather-permitting; peak billfish/dorado spring dry window (Mar-Jun sailfish/mahi); confirm species per season with operator","sargassum_window":"Apr-Aug (Jun-Jul peak); marina/inlet + dive focus softens beach dependence","booking_window_lead_time":"peak 3-4 months (gated villa/condo stock finite, book earlier); shoulder 4-6 months","holiday_event_peaks":["Christmas/New Year","Spring Break (Mar)","Semana Santa"],"fill_the_beds":"sargassum/green months lead with near-shore reef dives, Cenote Azul, Dolphin Discovery, sportfishing charters, marina promenade","campaign_start_trigger":"peak campaigns open Aug-Sep; shoulder ~3-4 months out; spring-sportfishing / dive-base push through sargassum months"},"jewels":[{"name":"Deep-water marina sportfishing charter","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"Half/full-day offshore charters from a rare mainland deep-water safe-haven harbor.","bookable_category":"fishing charter","source":"https://alohawanderers.com/puerto-aventuras-what-to-know-before-visiting-this-riviera-maya-gem/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Half/full-day offshore charters from a rare mainland deep-water safe-haven harbor.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 12%; berth fees pass-through"},{"name":"Dolphin Discovery swim","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Sea-inlet swims with dolphins, sea lions and manatees beside the marina.","bookable_category":"marine wildlife experience","source":"https://www.dolphindiscovery.com/riviera-maya/riviera-maya.asp","si":"wildlife","blurb":"Sea-inlet swims with dolphins, sea lions and manatees beside the marina.","commission":"brand affiliate; park entry pass-through"},{"name":"Shore-adjacent reef dive (reef ~100 ft out)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Near-shore reef dives with minimal transit — several dives in a day.","bookable_category":"reef dive","source":"https://www.prodiveinternational.com/diving/mexico/puerto-aventuras/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Near-shore reef dives with minimal transit — several dives in a day.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator affiliate / DMC 12%"},{"name":"Cenote Azul cavern dive/snorkel","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Popular cenote between Puerto Aventuras and Playa — cave country from a marina base.","bookable_category":"cenote cavern dive (guide required)","source":"https://alohawanderers.com/puerto-aventuras-what-to-know-before-visiting-this-riviera-maya-gem/","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Popular cenote between Puerto Aventuras and Playa — cave country from a marina base.","commission":"DMC 12% / affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Dreams Aventuras Riviera Maya","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"Secure, calm gated-community all-inclusive honeymoon base.","bookable_category":"all-inclusive resort","source":"https://www.trivago.com/en-US/oar/resort-dreams-aventuras-riviera-maya-puerto-aventuras","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Secure, calm gated-community all-inclusive honeymoon base.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"all-inclusive AOR ~12%"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Puerto Aventuras?","a":"Water, mosquitoes, hurricanes and sargassum — not crime. Drink bottled/purified water, use repellent for dengue (peak May–November, no malaria in tourist Quintana Roo), and note hurricane season runs June–November. Sargassum is heavy region-wide in 2026 (Apr–Aug), but the marina and dive focus soften the beach hit here.","source":"cdc.gov / deeparrival.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is the marina and sportfishing like in Puerto Aventuras?","a":"It is one of the few mainland deep-water marinas between Cancún and Belize City — a secure safe-haven harbor for yachts, sailors and sportfishers. Offshore charters run year-round (weather permitting), with the peak billfish and mahi window in the Mar–Jun spring dry season; berth fees are pass-through and the guided charter is the commissionable wrapper.","source":"alohawanderers.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is Puerto Aventuras a good dive base?","a":"Yes — it is a genuine near-shore reef and cenote base. The reef is only ~100 feet from the beach, so you can log several dives a day with minimal boat transit, and Cenote Azul (between Puerto Aventuras and Playa del Carmen) puts cave country within easy reach. Best reef visibility runs Nov–May.","source":"prodiveinternational.com / alohawanderers.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Puerto Aventuras good for families?","a":"Very — it is built for calm, safe family days. The adjacent Dolphin Discovery center offers sea-inlet swims with bottlenose dolphins, sea lions and manatees; add the gated 24/7-security layout, a calm marina promenade and near-shore reef, and it suits families and multigenerational groups well.","source":"dolphindiscovery.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"Is Puerto Aventuras good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, for couples who want secure and quiet over party energy. The in-community options are the branded all-inclusive Dreams Aventuras and private gated marina/golf villas with chef and concierge; the wider luxury tier runs ~US$400–600+/night in March. For branded ultra, Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree) is ~30–40 min north with an easy marina/dive day trip.","source":"machupicchu.org / trivago.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can I do Maya ruins from Puerto Aventuras?","a":"Yes — Tulum and Cobá are easy guided day trips, alongside Akumal''s turtle bay ~10 min south. Amstar and other Riviera Maya DMCs run cenote, Tulum-ruins and Akumal-turtle excursions from Puerto Aventuras; entries are pass-through, with the guided excursion the commissionable wrapper.","source":"embracethejourneytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Puerto Aventuras?","a":"December–April is peak (best weather, highest rates); the value windows are the May–June and November shoulders at ~30–40% off, with November clear of sargassum. The green season (Jun–mid-Oct) is hot, rainy and cheapest with hurricane exposure — but the marina and dive product hold up better than a pure beach stay.","source":"machupicchu.org / travelswithelle.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Puerto Aventuras Travel Guide 2026 — Marina, Reef Diving & Dolphins | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Puerto Aventuras: a gated deep-water marina town with reef 100 ft from shore, cenote diving, dolphin swims and sportfishing, plus 2026 sargassum, Level 2 safety and dive-chamber info.","slug":"puerto-aventuras-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Puerto Aventuras","marina Puerto Aventuras","buceo en Puerto Aventuras","Dolphin Discovery Puerto Aventuras","pesca deportiva Puerto Aventuras","villas en Puerto Aventuras","Cenote Azul Puerto Aventuras","es seguro Puerto Aventuras"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private gated marina/golf villas","price_tier":"luxury","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / host or luxury-DMC villa AOR","mor_posture":true,"note":"top of in-community ladder; no true ultra hotel in-community","source":"https://www.rentalescapes.com/rentals/luxury-vacation-rentals-mexico/riviera-maya/puerto-aventuras"},{"name":"Dreams Aventuras Riviera Maya","price_tier":"premier","virtuoso":false,"earning":"all-inclusive AOR ~12% (Hyatt Inclusive/host)","mor_posture":true,"note":"top hotel SKU in-community, not true ultra","source":"https://www.trivago.com/en-US/oar/resort-dreams-aventuras-riviera-maya-puerto-aventuras"},{"name":"Rosewood Mayakoba (~30-40 min north)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"note":"nearest true ultra hotel","source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"Banyan Tree / Andaz-Alila Mayakoba","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"La Casa de la Playa (Grupo Xcaret)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"15% via Xcaret Agents Pro OR host-Virtuoso ($100 credit)","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/hotels/16561922/la-casa-de-la-playa"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Puerto Aventuras, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.4986,"lng":-87.2261}}'::jsonb, 26)
